{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sports and Leisure"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "After the Fall"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le02ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Non-Defining Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use relative clauses to join two separate clauses into one sentence. You can also use relative clauses to give more information about something. </br>A non-defining relative clause gives us extra information about a noun. You don't need this information to know which noun we are talking about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A non-defining relative clause can either be used as subject or object. You can't drop the relative pronoun in this kind of clause. </br>You cannot use <span class=\"italic\">that</span> in a non-defining relative clause, but always <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for an object and <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for a person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A non-defining relative clause can come after the subject.</br> Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">Danielle, who was an expert climber, broke both her legs in a climbing accident. </br>The hospital, which specializes in mountaineering injuries, was two hours away by helicopter. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A non-defining relative clause can come after the object. </br>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">The doctors spoke with Danielle, who looked to be in a lot of pain. </br>The doctors thought it was an amazing recovery, which is extremely rare with this type of injuries.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Danielle, who had always had an tenacious spirit, was determined to walk again."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I now have to pay more attention and put less weight on my left foot, which is permanently weaker."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Several years ago, Danielle, who is an expert climber, survived a fall from one of the tallest mountain peaks in Alaska."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She spent over a year in the local hospital, which specializes in mountaineering injuries, and then several months in a wheelchair."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbial Clause of Place"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "An adverbial clause is a group of words which have the same function as an adverb. Like all clauses, an adverbial clause has a subject and a verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adverbial clauses of place are used to express where something happens. An adverb of place often starts often starts with a preposition like <span class=\"italic\">in</span>, <span class=\"italic\">on</span> or <span class=\"italic\">near</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use a subordinating conjunction like <span class=\"italic\">anywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">everywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">where</span> or <span class=\"italic\">wherever</span> to introduce the adverbial clause. </br>Example:</br><span class=\"italic\">Danielle tries to climb a mountain wherever she travels to. She is willing to travel anywhere mountains can be found.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "In a world where there is so much pessimism, she never once lost her positive outlook."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Everywhere she goes, people ask her how she manages to do it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She is willing to go anywhere good climbing can be found. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She is back on the mountain and enters competitions wherever she travels."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "persistence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of continuing to put forth an effort"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Danielle claims her success is due to dedication and persistence. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about adventurous activities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to scale"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to climb"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She was scaling a steep cliff with two other enthusiasts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "enthusiast"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who is very interested in a particular subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The climbing enthusiasts met every week to practice. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grip"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to hold something very tightly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She lost her grip and fell."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tenacious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unwilling to accept defeat; persistent "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Danielle, who had always had an tenacious spirit, was determined to walk again."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fulfil"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to complete something that was planned or expected"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Today, Danielle is fulfilling her dream."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dedication"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to give a lot of time and energy to something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Danielle claims her success is due to dedication and persistence. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research adventurous moments in history."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create sentences in the past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use relative clauses. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my work with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research ten adventurous accomplishments."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a sentence to describe each one (i.e. Neil Armstrong walked on the moon.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Insert some extra information into each one by adding a relative clause (e.g. Neil Armstrong, who was from the United States, walked on the moon)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your ten sentences to a partner. "}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn10le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn10le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "Several years ago, Danielle, who is an expert climber, survived a fall from one of the tallest mountain peaks in Alaska. She had been scaling a steep cliff with two other enthusiasts when she lost her grip and fell. She was told at the time that her injuries, which were quite severe, might prevent her from ever walking again. She had broken her hip bone and had only limited movement in her left foot.", "id": 1}, {"time": "26000", "image": "engenn10le02ob07re2img02.jpg", "text": "Danielle, who had always had a tenacious spirit, was determined to walk again. She spent over a year in the local hospital, which specializes in mountaineering injuries, and then several months in a wheelchair. In a world where there is so much pessimism, she never once lost her positive outlook. Her recovery was slow, but one and a half years after the accident, Danielle was able to stand on her feet and walk. The doctors thought it was a remarkable recovery. But for Danielle, walking was not enough. She dreamed of climbing again.", "id": 2}, {"time": "60000", "image": "engenn10le02ob07re2img03.jpg", "text": "Today, Danielle is fulfilling her dream. She is back on the mountain and enters competitions wherever she travels, and she is willing to go anywhere good climbing can be found.\n</br>\nEverywhere she goes, people ask her how she manages to do it. Danielle claims her success is due to dedication and persistence. She says, \"I never gave up. I exercise as often as I can and always look for opportunities to climb. I've also had to learn to climb differently. I now have to pay more attention and put less weight on my left foot, which is permanently weaker. All in all, I have become a better climber as a result of the accident!\"", "id": 3}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le02ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le02ob07re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1}], "id": 0, "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about sports and leisure time."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express complex statements using words like <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span>. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about where something is done. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Have you ever had an accident or injury when doing a sport? What happened?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Which adventurous activities have you tried? "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's meet an adventurous character!"}], "id": 0}, {"type": "STI", "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Danielle gets <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">back on the horse</span>."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text